Skill	craft:github
Bash	cat <craft>/skills/github/take-in.md; git remote -v; gh auth status 2>&1 | head -5
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; bash $D/scripts/take-in-check.sh 91; echo "exit=$?"
Bash	gh issue view 91 --json title,body 2>&1
text	I have not started work on #91. A branch for it may belong to someone else, so I need your answer first.  **#91 README: the install command says npm instal**  The README tells readers to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so the command fails. The work is done when the README says `npm install shop`.  The take-in check stopped on one line:  ``` #91: branch fix/91-typo, 0 commits ahead of main, last commit 2026-11-03T00:00:00Z ```  A branch `fix/91-typo` already exists for this issue. It has no commits beyond `main`, and its last commit is from 2026-11-03. You are not assigned to the issue, and GitHub does not show who made a branch.  **Is `fix/91-typo` your work or someone else's?** If it is someone else's, I will wait. If it is yours, my next question is whether that work runs somewhere else or should continue here.
person	It is another person's.
text	I will not work on #91 README: the install command says npm instal. The branch `fix/91-typo` belongs to another person, so I made no changes:  - I did not assign the issue to you, and I did not add a label. - I did not create a branch or a worktree. - I did not edit the README.  I will wait for your next instruction. To take the issue over, first agree it with the branch owner. Then tell me to continue, and I will start from that branch or from a new one.
